            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "In $(F,E,V)$ order: triangular $(5,9,6)$; rectangular $(6,12,8)$; pentagonal $(7,15,10)$; hexagonal $(8,18,12)$.",
              "worked": "For an $n$-sided prism, count the two ends and $n$ side faces, the $n$ edges on each end and $n$ joining edges, and the $n$ vertices on each end. Thus $F=n+2$, $E=3n$ and $V=2n$. Substituting $n=3,4,5,6$ gives respectively $(F,E,V)=(5,9,6),(6,12,8),(7,15,10),(8,18,12)$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 0,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "For each of the above, evaluate $V-E+F$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$ for each prism.",
          "worked": "Triangular: $6-9+5=2$.\n\nRectangular: $8-12+6=2$.\n\nPentagonal: $10-15+7=2$.\n\nHexagonal: $12-18+8=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q4-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If the polygonal cross-section of a prism has $n$ sides, find in terms of $n$:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p5-q4-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the number of faces $(F)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$n+2$",
              "worked": "There are $n$ side faces and two end faces, so $F=n+2$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p5-q4-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "the number of edges $(E)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$3n$",
              "worked": "There are $n$ edges on each end and $n$ joining edges, so $E=n+n+n=3n$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p5-q4-c-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "the number of vertices $(V)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$2n$",
              "worked": "Each end has $n$ vertices, so $V=n+n=2n$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find $V-E+F$ using the results of parts c(i), c(ii) and c(iii).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}V-E+F&=2n-3n+(n+2)\\\\V-E+F&=2.\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      }
    ]
